<title>USA: Bankers Trust files shelf for $500 mln debt.</title>
<headline>Bankers Trust files shelf for $500 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankers Trust New York Corporation said Wednesday it filed a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $500 million in debt.</p>
<p>The registration includes junior subordinated debentures due 2036 and trust preferred securities, the filing said.  </p>
<p>Proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes, the filing said.</p>
<p>Bankers Trust New York Corp is a bank holding company, incorporated under the laws of the state of New York in 1965.</p>
